      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f1613de4-3bc7-5b58-be60-ceb37e1bd10c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Gaillardia, Browningia, Helenium\n- Taxonomy: Asteraceae, Helenieae, Helianthodae, Anthroismeae, Coreopsideae, Eupatorieae, Heliantheae, Inuleae, Tageteae\n\nFacts:\n- Gaillardia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Asteraceae and is commonly called blanket flower.\n- Gaillardia is native to North and South America.\n- Browningia is a genus of cacti with 11 accepted species and 3 unresolved species.\n- In the tribe Helenieae, Helenium is the type genus.\n- In the tribe Helenieae, Gaillardia is among the best known members.\n- Helianthodae is a supertribe in the family Asteraceae.\n- Helianthodae contains the tribes Anthroismeae, Coreopsideae, Eupatorieae, Helenieae, Heliantheae, Inuleae, and Tageteae.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8318aa52-77a2-550f-b73f-80ffdf82ea2d",
        "text": "Page: Gaillardia. Sentence: Gaillardia (common name blanket flower) is a genus of flowering plants in the sunflower family, Asteraceae, native to North and South America.\nPage: Browningia. Sentence: Browningia is a genus of cacti, comprising 11 accepted and 3 unresolved species.\nPage: Helenieae. Sentence: The type genus is \"Helenium\", but the best known members of the tribe are the \"Gaillardia\".\nPage: Helianthodae. Sentence: Helianthodae is a supertribe in the family Asteraceae, the aster family, containing the tribes Anthroismeae, Coreopsideae, Eupatorieae, Helenieae, Heliantheae, Inuleae, and Tageteae.",
